  "content": {
    "The ISWG developed a conceptual framework using Multilevel Approaches Toward Community Health (MATCH) to define four levels where guideline implementation strategies can be initiated: policy level, clinical institution level, provider level, and patient level. The current taxonomy, derived from the Cochrane Effective Practice and Organisation of Care (EPOC) Group, includes Professional Interventions, Financial Interventions, Organizational Interventions, and Regulatory Interventions. The ISWG used an Rx for Change database to review existing systematic reviews on healthcare implementation strategies, identifying three strategies with some evidence of effectiveness: academic detailing, audit and feedback, and provider reminders. A fourth strategy, provider incentives, was also included based on evidence from Europe and U.S. healthcare systems.": 20
